** AMR + rigid-contact integration test (PLAN_AMR_CONTACT.md §5/P4 test): a single C3D20 block sits
** against an analytic rigid wall at its own left face (nodeToRigidSurfacePenalty, component=0,
** direction=-1, value=0.0), watching nSet 'gen_left'. The block is refined mid-run by hAdaptivity
** while the right face is being pushed left, compressing the block against the wall. Exercises
** Constraint.reconcile(): the refined left face gains new boundary nodes (face-interior +
** edge-midpoints of the octree split) that must be picked up into the watched node set and
** protected from penetrating the wall -- before PLAN_AMR_CONTACT.md's P4, they would silently stay
** unprotected (never added to the frozen slaveNodes list from construction).
*material, name=linearelastic, id=mat
30000, 0.15

*section, name=sec, material=mat, type=solid
all

*modelGenerator, generator=boxGen, name=gen
nX      =1
nY      =1
nZ      =1
lX      =1
lY      =1
lZ      =1
elType  =C3D20

*constraint, type=nodetorigidsurfacepenalty, name=wall
nSet=gen_left
field=displacement
component=0
penalty=1e6
value=0.0
direction=-1
type=linear

*modelModifier, type=hAdaptivity, name=amr
result=stress
expression='x > 300.0'
reducer=absmax
maxLevel=1

*job, name=amrrigid, domain=3d
*solver, solver=NIST, name=theSolver
*fieldOutput
>>perNode, elSet=all, field=displacement, result=U, name=U

*step, solver=theSolver
maxInc=0.02, minInc=1e-6, maxNumInc=100, maxIter=25, stepLength=1
>>options, category=NISTSolver, extrapolation=off
>>dirichlet, name=fixBottomLeftFront, nSet=gen_bottomLeftFront, field=displacement, 2=0.0, 3=0.0
>>dirichlet, name=fixBottomLeftBack, nSet=gen_bottomLeftBack, field=displacement, 2=0.0
>>dirichlet, name=pushRight, nSet=gen_right, field=displacement, 1=-0.1
